<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Evaluation on SD v1.5.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assess <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> on the pre-trained Stable Diffusion v1.5 (SD v1.5) using the modified LAION-mi benchmark (see <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> for details). As demonstrated in <a href="#S5.T3" title="In 5.3 Evaluation on Stable Diffusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, prior methods suffer notable performance degradation when conditioned on VLM-generated captions. In contrast, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> outperforms all VLM-conditioned baselines and even surpasses the GT-captioned CLiD in ASR. Although its AUC is slightly lower, it achieves the highest TPR@1%FPR, exceeding the second-best result by over 20%, demonstrating strong discriminative power in high-precision regimes. We include additional experiments on SD v2.1 (<a href="#A1.SS9.SSS2" title="A.9.2 Stable Diffusion v2.1 ‣ A.9 Evaluation against Stable Diffusion v1.5, v2.1, and v3 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9.2</span></a>) with a different text encoder and SD v3 with a fundamentally different architecture (<a href="#A1.SS9.SSS3" title="A.9.3 Stable Diffusion v3 ‣ A.9 Evaluation against Stable Diffusion v1.5, v2.1, and v3 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Understanding the Separability of <span id="S5.SS4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span></h3>

<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:48%;"><img src="2602.22689v1/COCO_score_2.png" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:267/149;" width="267" height="149" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>(a) Membership score distributions when conditioned on the model-fitted embedding <math id="S5.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. (b) <math id="S5.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> for member and hold-out samples under varying conditions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We attribute the performance gain of <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> to the distinct sensitivity characteristics between member and hold-out samples.
Interestingly, this disparity is further amplified when conditioning on the model-fitted embedding <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As observed in the MS-COCO dataset (<a href="#S5.F3" title="In 5.4 Understanding the Separability of MoFit ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(b, top)), member samples exhibit a pronounced increase in <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating a strong sensitivity to the misaligned condition. In contrast, hold-out samples exhibit only a modest increase – their <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> distribution closely aligned with that under other conditions (<a href="#S5.F3" title="In 5.4 Understanding the Separability of MoFit ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(b, bottom)).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As a result, when computing the final discrepancy score <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{{MoFit} }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</mtext><mtext> </mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{{MoFit} }}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S4.E7" title='In 4.3 Membership Inference with Amplified ℒ_"cond" Disparity ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) in <a href="#S5.F3" title="In 5.4 Understanding the Separability of MoFit ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(a), member samples predominantly exhibit positive values due to the pronounced gap between <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, hold-out samples yield scores near zero, suggesting minimal impact from the change in conditioning. Results of Pokemon and Flickr datasets are depicted in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 MoFit on Pokemon and Flickr ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate <math id="S5.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further evaluate the effectiveness of <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}+\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}+\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we perform an ablation by varying the input image used to extract the embedding <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we compare four configurations: (i) the original query image <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> – corresponding to the alternative described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, (ii) the query image with random noise <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}+\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, (iii) an adversarial variant <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}+\delta_{\text{MAX}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>MAX</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}+\delta_{\text{MAX}}</annotation></semantics></math> optimized to <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">maximize</span> <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Model-Fitted Surrogate Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and (iv) our proposed surrogate <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}+\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}+\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, which minimizes <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Model-Fitted Surrogate Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
For configuration (ii), we add uniformly sampled noise drawn from the range <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-\varepsilon,\varepsilon]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-\varepsilon,\varepsilon]</annotation></semantics></math> to the query image, and for each dataset, we sweep <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\{0.1,0.2,\ldots,0.9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\{0.1,0.2,\ldots,0.9\}</annotation></semantics></math>, reporting the results at the best-performing noise level (<math id="S5.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pokemon</span>, <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MS-COCO</span>, and <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Flickr</span>).
Importantly, for (iii), while <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> constructs a model-fitted pair <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{0}^{*},\phi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{0}^{*},\phi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> that is tightly coupled and mutually adapted to the target model, <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\text{MAX}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mtext>MAX</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\text{MAX}}</annotation></semantics></math> forces the query <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to explicitly deviate from the model’s learned distribution.</p>
</div>
