<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Quantitative comparison of MIA performance under input image variations.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S5.T4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> outperforms all alternative input types, underscoring the importance of extracting <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from a surrogate <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that is carefully aligned with the model’s learned representation. This pairing forms a mutually adapted structure: <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is tailored to tightly conform to the model, and <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> captures this overfitted signal with high fidelity.
While random noise <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> offers modest discriminative signals in specific cases (e.g., Pokemon), its performance lacks consistency across different datasets.
In contrast, <span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> achieves stable and superior results in all evaluation metrics and datasets, demonstrating robust generalization to variations in training data.
Membership score distributions for each dataset are provided in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Input image variations ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, and additional ablation studies are detailed in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:45%;"><img src="2602.22689v1/Discussion_1.png" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:248/188;" width="248" height="188" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Distributions of (left) <math id="S5.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and (right) <math id="S5.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> of member and hold-out pairs from (a) Pokemon dataset and (b) model-fitted pairs of <span id="S5.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.6 </span>Discussions</h3>

<section id="S5.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.6.1 </span>Overfitting degree of surrogate–embedding pairs</h4>

<div id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess whether the two-stage optimization in <span id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> effectively overfits both the surrogate image <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding embedding <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we examine the distributions of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> computed by the target model. Specifically, we compare these loss values for ground-truth image-caption pairs <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> and our model-fitted pairs <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{*},\phi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{*},\phi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a) illustrates the loss distributions of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> from the Pokemon dataset. In <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(b, left), we present the <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> values of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> where it corresponds to the outcome of the surrogate optimization stage (<a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Model-Fitted Surrogate Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) in <span id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span>. Notably, the <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> values of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are significantly lower than those of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the surrogate has been strongly overfitted to the model’s unconditional prior.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(b, right), we observe a further decrease in <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> following the embedding optimization stage (<a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Surrogate-Driven Embedding Extraction ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), where the embedding <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is specifically tailored to pair with the surrogate <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compared to the <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> distribution of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a, right), the loss values of <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{*},\phi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{*},\phi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> are not only substantially lower but also more concentrated – exhibiting significantly reduced variance. This suggests that <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is highly aligned with the surrogate <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> on the model’s learned manifold.
This strong alignment is expected to induce substantial mismatch when <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied to the original query image <math id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby amplifying the sensitivity of member samples during membership inference.
Corresponding loss distributions for other datasets are provided in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5 Handling Unknown Membership via Surrogate Overfitting ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This uniform overfitting serves as a critical foundation: once the surrogate and its embedding is overfitted and tightly aligned, the embedding can more effectively separate members from hold-outs, as evidenced by the improved performance of <span id="S5.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> in <a href="#S5.T4" title="In 5.5 Effectiveness of Model-Fitted Surrogate 𝑥_0^∗ ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.6.2 </span>Potential Defensive Method</h4>

