<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional implementation details to improve the reproducibility and clarity of our experimental setup.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Optimization Details &amp; Ablation Study.</span> We iteratively optimize the perturbation <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> in the direction of the gradient sign. Specifically, the perturbation is uniformly sample from the range <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.3,0.3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.3,0.3]</annotation></semantics></math> and is updated via following equation:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i+1}=x^{\prime}_{i}-\alpha\cdot\text{sign}(\nabla_{x^{\prime}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>sign</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i+1}=x^{\prime}_{i}-\alpha\cdot\text{sign}(\nabla_{x^{\prime}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the unconditional loss defined in <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Model-Fitted Surrogate Optimization ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the surrogate being optimized at iteration <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The step size <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to 0.15 and proportionally decayed with the iteration count.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To justify the choice of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we conduct a hyperparameter analysis across multiple values: <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in\{0.025,0.05,0.1,0.2,0.3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.025</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in\{0.025,0.05,0.1,0.2,0.3\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We perform this analysis on the Pokemon dataset by randomly sampling 100 images from both the member and hold-out sets. As shown in <a href="#A1.F5" title="In A.1 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, increasing <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> generally improves attack performance up to a certain point, with both ASR and AUC peaking at <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.15</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on this observation, we use <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.15</annotation></semantics></math> throughout all experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting model-fitted surrogate is then used to extract an embedding via the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 0.06. The number of optimization steps varies by dataset: 200 steps for Pokemon, 300 steps for MS-COCO and Flickr, and 1000 steps for Stable Diffusion v1.5. The increased iteration count for Stable Diffusion is due to its strong generalization, which requires more steps to be overfitted.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:64%;"><img src="2602.22689v1/ASR_AUC.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:354/159;" width="354" height="159" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>ASR and AUC for different initial step size and timestep <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For a single query image, the overall runtime for its two-stage optimization process varies by dataset: approximately 7 minutes for Pokemon, 8 minutes for MS-COCO and Flickr, and 9 minutes for Stable Diffusion v1.5, all measured on a single NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 GPU. Please refer to <a href="#A1.SS8.SSS1" title="A.8.1 Optimizer-Specific VRAM Usage and Runtime ‣ A.8 Runtime of MoFit and Early Stopping Strategy ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8.1</span></a> for more details.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Both optimization procedures are performed at a fixed diffusion timestep of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=140" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=140</annotation></semantics></math>, within the full denoising schedule of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1000</annotation></semantics></math>. This choice is guided by ablation results presented in <a href="#A1.F5" title="In A.1 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, where ASR and AUC are evaluated across varying timesteps ranging from <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=50</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=700" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>700</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=700</annotation></semantics></math>. The results indicate that performance peaks within the range <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[100,200]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>100,200</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[100,200]</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, we adopt <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=140" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=140</annotation></semantics></math> for all experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Membership Inference.</span> For the auxiliary loss <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{aux}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aux</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{aux}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.E9" title='In 4.3 Membership Inference with Amplified ℒ_"cond" Disparity ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we use <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> for Pokemon and Stable Diffusion v1.5, and use <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{VLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{VLM}}</annotation></semantics></math> for MS-COCO and Flickr. The balancing hyperparameter <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is increased by 0.05 within the range <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is selected to maximize ASR for each <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> All baseline methods are evaluated using their default settings. For the Naive method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Matsumoto et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, membership is determined based on <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For SecMI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Duan et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and PIA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, we adopt the SecMI-stat and the default PIA, respectively – both rely on threshold-based inference without training a classification model.
When ground-truth captions are available, CLiD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> proposes several caption-splitting strategies (<span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, simple clipping, random noise, and word importance calculation). Among them, we adopt simple clipping. Unlike CLiD, <span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MoFit</span> follows the settings of SecMI and PIA, assuming access to a subset of member and hold-out samples for threshold calibration; hence, we do not train a shadow model to determine <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target Models.</span> We evaluate our method on a range of text-to-image diffusion models trained on diverse datasets. We begin with SD-Pokemon, introduced in <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Observations ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ No Caption, No Problem: Caption-Free Membership Inference via Model-Fitted Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, which fine-tunes Stable Diffusion v1.4 on 416/417 member/hold-out image-caption pairs for 15,000 steps. Using the same base model, we further fine-tune on 2,500/2,458 splits of MS-COCO and 2,500/2,500 splits of Flickr, each with 150,000 steps, following the experimental setups in prior studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Duan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhai et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:50%;">
<div id="A1.T6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:199.2pt;height:76.1pt;vertical-align:-36.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-28.7pt,11.0pt) scale(0.776234820828147,0.776234820828147) ;">
<table id="A1.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Methods</span></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T6.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Condition</span></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">LAION-mi</td></tr>
